From: Jordan Bettcher <thebettcher@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] linux: never build the jni FFI plugin into the desktop bundle

Class:   LOCAL WORKAROUND (packaging hygiene; same as ours/localsend 0003).
Applies: open-chess v1.3.0 (patch -p1 from the repository root).
Fixes:   jni 1.0.5 (transitive, via path_provider_android 2.3.1) is a Linux
         ffiPlugin, so generated_plugins.cmake always add_subdirectory()s it,
         and with a JDK on the build host it builds libdartjni.so with NEEDED
         libjvm.so and a RUNPATH into /usr/lib/jvm. Nothing on Linux loads it.
---
--- a/linux/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/linux/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -70,6 +70,12 @@
 )
 
 
+# The `jni` FFI plugin (pulled in by path_provider_android) is Android-only in
+# practice, but on Linux it builds libdartjni.so linked against libjvm.so,
+# with a RUNPATH into /usr/lib/jvm, whenever the build host has a JDK. Keep
+# that out of the bundle.
+set(CMAKE_DISABLE_FIND_PACKAGE_JNI TRUE)
+
 # Generated plugin build rules, which manage building the plugins and adding
 # them to the application.
 include(flutter/generated_plugins.cmake)
